//! fail
//! error-any: unexpected character '#'
// A lone CR is whitespace and ends no line (D2.1). An error after it drops the tokens before
// it too, so the parser sees no half statement and line 9 gives 1 error (D14.2). The harness
// reads a lone CR as a line end, so the error-any line and the golden hold the error with its
// line and column.
fn main() i32 {
    println("a");
    i32 x = 1 +# 2;
    return 0;
}
